&lt;p&gt;Russian President Vladimir Putin has agreed to resume US-mediated peace talks with Ukraine as early as next month, the Kremlin said on Wednesday, following a meeting with US envoy Steve Witkoff in St Petersburg. The discussions mark Washington's latest attempt to end Europe's deadliest conflict since World War II.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The meeting, Witkoff's ninth in-person encounter with Putin, began with a goodwill gesture from Moscow. Russia released Stephen Hubbard, a retired American schoolteacher who had been detained in the country, following a request from US President Donald Trump.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The talks took place amid growing concerns in Kyiv and among its allies that Washington is stepping back from its support for Ukraine. The United States has, at times, withheld real-time intelligence on Russian attacks and disrupted Ukraine's military communications, raising questions about its continued commitment to Kyiv.&lt;/p&gt;
